/-!
# Adelic Krein Geometry

Umbrella for the index theory of Hermitian states on the dilation–translation system of `ℚ` and of
its places.

* Index calculus on groups: induced states, witness complements and escape, mixing and height decay,
  twin-blindness, block additivity.
* Arithmetic types: the affine zero-or-infinity law, the Kakutani wall as an index wall and its locality
  (the same wall at every prime, the product formula), Weil's affine extensions, the running
  counterterm of the prime kernel, archimedean continuity against height decay, the adelic product
  state.
* Additive side: the additive and Ramanujan index laws on `ℤ/N` and `ℚ/ℤ`, conditionally positive
  successors (`−|b|`, `−|b|^s`, ultrametric `−|b|_v`, `−|·|_∞` on `F[X]`).
* Conformal and pole structure: conformal symmetry costs one square; the pole as a Krein state;
  conformal induction and the pole–successor states over any field and place, their signature formula
  `κ = κ₀(ψ) + 1`, additivity over places, shell decompositions.
* Gluing at the archimedean place: the boost-polar index, the gluing formula `κ = κ^{(½)}(K) + 1`, free
  hyperplanes for sub-boost and periodic data, prime towers, Jordan pair kernels on dilations
  `κ(Σ_i J_{u_i, P_i}) = Σ_i (deg P_i + 1)`, the count `κ = #{zeros right of the line} + 1` for Weil's
  archimedean state and for Dirichlet L-functions, and the source-defined heat-deformed archimedean
  state `φ_c^{(t)}` of `H_t` (`κ(φ_c^{(t)}) = #{nonreal right zeros of H_t with mult} + 1 < ⊤` for all
  `t > 0`, lower semicontinuous, nonincreasing, jumping by `1` per collided pair); the gluing square is
  sharp, absorbs the simple pole pair at any strength and charges a double pole; the stable gluing
  formula at exponent `0 < s < 1`, whose absorbed pair sits at `(1 ± s)/2`, and every other real pair
  costs its square; the local wall over `𝔽_q(X)` at the place `∞`; the additive reading of a glued
  state has one square and the two readings add; the signature formula
  `Σ_p κ₀(k_p) + 1 ≤ κ ≤ Σ_p κ₀(k_p) + 2` for finitely many prime towers glued at `∞`; the gluing
  formula at every place and every gluing successor, and Weil's correlation glued at every prime with
  `κ = #{zeros right of the line} + 1`; the shell identity of the archimedean Weil form.
* Haar carriers (`Haar/`): index preservation by positive integer-successor carriers, axis-invisible
  kernels and their degree and rank laws, period defects, and infinite index for every Haar kernel
  with a continuous dilation reading.
* Tower coupling (`TowerCoupling/`): exact polar second-difference identity `κ₀(k) = κ(Δ²k)` and
  `{0, 1, ⊤}` polar trichotomy on `ℤ`; impossibility of capturing `κ(K_ζ) + 1` via separable
  `S`-truncated explicit-formula prime-tower assemblies (finite local polar indices count only pole
  shares and are blind to `S`-primes and Gamma; pole-retaining cubic-spline assemblies diverge
  `≥ |S| + 1 → ⊤`; pole-free assemblies lie in `{1, 2, ⊤}` whereas `κ(weilArchState c) ≠ 2`;
  diagonal counterterms collapse both `Λ` and its single-prime flip to glued index `1`); coprime
  cross-difference rigidity blocking pointwise approximation of `ratCorr` by arbitrary separable
  tower assemblies and forcing axial replication blow-up on `0 < κ(K_ζ) < ⊤`; and two unconditional
  coupled local-to-global signature formulas (`coupledAssembly S ratCorr` for `|S| ≥ 2`, and
  window-coupled `sTruncatedCorr S` with zero counterterm on `|log |slope|| ≤ L`, `S ⊇ windowPrimes L`).

See `AdelicKreinGeometry/README.md`.
-/
